159 - The Old Rugged Cross
 / 
Key: Ab
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 159
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[Ab]On a hill far away stood an [Db]old rugged cross,
[Bb]The [Eb7]emblem of suffering and [Ab]shame,
[Ab]And I love that old cross where the [Db]dearest and best
[Bb]For a [Eb7]world of lost sinners was [Ab]slain.
[Eb7]So I'll cherish the old rugged [Ab]cross,
Till my [Db]trophies at last I lay [Ab]down;
I will cling to the old rugged [Db]cross,
And [Ab]exchange it some [Eb7]day for a [Ab]crown.

Refrain:
[Ab]So I'll cherish [Db]the old rugged cross,
[Bb]till my [Eb7]trophies at last [Ab]I lay down;
[Ab]I will cling to [Db]the old rugged cross,
[Bb]and exchange [Eb7]it some day [Ab]for a crown.

Verse 2:
[Ab]O that old rugged cross, [Db]so despised by the world,
[Bb]has a [Eb7]wondrous attraction [Ab]for me;
[Ab]for the dear Lamb of [Db]God left his glory above
[Bb]to bear [Eb7]it to [Ab]dark Calvary.

Verse 3:
[Ab]To that old rugged cross [Db]I will ever be true,
[Bb]its shame [Eb7]and reproach [Ab]gladly bear;
[Ab]then he'll call me some [Db]day to my home far away,
[Bb]where his [Eb7]glory forever [Ab]I'll share.
